Add selectable k-means backends for vector palettization (`cluster_dim > 1`): `cuml`, `flash_kmeans`, `sklearn` and `sklearn_minibatch` alongside the existing torch `kmeans++`, selected via `COREAI_KMEANS_BACKEND`. Add a batched clustering path that clusters every block of a weight tensor in one call rather than one call per block and expose the seeding and Lloyd stages as separately timed, independently swappable functions (`generate_init_seeds`, `run_lloyd_batched`).
